# The UFS LUNs (sda-sdf) hold ~100 Android partitions. Each one, with its
# /dev/disk/by-* symlinks, became its own .device unit (687 dev-disk-* units
# of 951 in all) that PID 1 had to create and track, and PID 1 is single
# threaded: it ran at 100% of a core for the whole boot, which is why units
# started in bursts. Only two keep the tag: persist, which
# (tqftpserv-populate-readwrite) is ordered against, and userdata, where an
# install on UFS has its root (crypttab and fstab wait on its by-uuid device,
# and without the tag that wait runs out: "start job for
# /dev/disk/by-uuid/..."). The symlinks themselves stay, for the
# ConditionPathExists= checks on them. Must sort after 99-systemd.rules, which
# adds the tag.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sd[a-f]*", ENV{ID_PART_ENTRY_NAME}!="persist", ENV{ID_PART_ENTRY_NAME}!="userdata", TAG-="systemd"
